---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../data/site';

const op = LEGAL.operator;
const email = LEGAL.contactEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  path="/terms/"
  lede="The agreement between you and DummyLead: your subscription, acceptable use, billing, liability, and the rules that govern the service."
  description="DummyLead Terms of Service: subscription terms, customer compliance obligations for call recording, billing, warranties, liability, and governing law."
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service (the "Terms") are a binding agreement between you, or
    the company you represent ("you", "Customer"), and
    {op}, {LEGAL.operatorDescriptor}, operating
    the DummyLead service at <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> and
    <strong>{SITE.appUrl.replace('https://', '')}</strong> ("DummyLead", "we",
    "us"). By creating an account or using the service you agree to these Terms.
    If you do not agree, do not use the service.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead is a seed-lead monitoring tool. We create decoy "seed" lead
    identities, each with an inbox and a live phone line, that you place into a
    lead flow you control. We then capture and present the calls, texts, and
    emails that reach those seeds, along with derived signals such as response
    time, spam risk, and call attestation. You are responsible for how you place
    and use seeds and for the conclusions you draw from the data.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You must be at least 18 and able to form a binding contract. If you use
      DummyLead for an organization, you represent that you are authorized to
      bind it.
    </li>
    <li>
      You are responsible for the accuracy of your account information, for
      keeping your credentials secure, and for all activity under your account.
    </li>
    <li>Notify us promptly at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> of any unauthorized use.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Customer compliance: recording, consent, and lawful use</h2>
  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>This is the most important section. Read it.</strong> DummyLead
      records phone calls and captures messages. Laws on call recording and
      monitoring vary widely by country and by US state, and some require the
      consent of <strong>every</strong> party to a call ("two-party" or
      "all-party" consent). You, the Customer, are solely responsible for
      determining whether and how you may lawfully record, monitor, and use the
      interactions captured through your seeds.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>You represent, warrant, and agree that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You have all rights, consents, and lawful bases required to place seed
      leads and to record, store, transcribe, and use every call, text, and
      email they capture;
    </li>
    <li>
      You will comply with all applicable laws, including wiretapping,
      eavesdropping, call-recording, consent, telemarketing, anti-spam, and data
      protection laws in every jurisdiction where you, your seeds, and the people
      contacting them are located;
    </li>
    <li>
      You will use captured data only for legitimate auditing, quality, and
      compliance purposes, and not to harass, defraud, surveil unlawfully, or
      discriminate against any person;
    </li>
    <li>
      You will follow our <a href="/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a>,
      which is incorporated into these Terms.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You are the data controller for captured-interaction data; we process it on
    your behalf under Section 11 and our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Subscriptions, seeds, and billing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      DummyLead is billed as a subscription, priced per concurrent active seed,
      monthly, at the rates shown on our <a href="/#pricing">pricing</a> page.
      Some high-volume usage (for example, very high call volume) may be metered
      and shown before it bills.
    </li>
    <li>
      Fees are charged in advance for each billing cycle through our payment
      processor. By subscribing you authorize recurring charges until you cancel.
    </li>
    <li>
      Adding or retiring seeds changes your bill; tier rates apply automatically
      and changes are prorated to your cycle.
    </li>
    <li>
      Unless stated otherwise, fees are exclusive of taxes, and you are
      responsible for any applicable taxes other than taxes on our income.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may change pricing on a prospective basis with reasonable notice before
      your next renewal.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Cancellations and refunds are governed by our
    <a href="/refunds/">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You may not use DummyLead to break the law, infringe rights, send spam,
    stalk or harass, or interfere with the service's security or integrity. The
    full list of prohibitions is in the
    <a href="/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a>. We may suspend or
    terminate accounts that violate it.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    We own the DummyLead service, software, and brand. We grant you a limited,
    non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the service during your
    subscription. You own the data you submit and the reports generated for you;
    you grant us the rights needed to operate the service and to create
    aggregated, de-identified analytics that do not identify you or any
    individual.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead relies on third-party providers for telephony, messaging,
    transcription, hosting, and payments. Your use may be subject to their terms,
    and we are not responsible for their acts or omissions.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided "as is" and "as available". To the maximum extent
    permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including
    merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We
    do not warrant that captured data, transcripts, spam scores, or attestation
    grades are complete, accurate, or admissible as evidence, and DummyLead does
    not provide legal advice. You are responsible for verifying findings before
    acting on them.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, neither party is liable for indirect,
    incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits
    or data, arising from the service. Our total liability for any claim relating
    to the service is limited to the fees you paid us in the 12 months before the
    event giving rise to the claim. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain
    limitations, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You will defend, indemnify, and hold harmless DummyLead and
    {op} from claims, damages, and costs
    (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the service, your
    placement of seeds, your recording or use of captured interactions, or your
    breach of these Terms or of any law, including call-recording and consent
    laws.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Data processing</h2>
  <p>
    Where we process personal data on your behalf (captured-interaction data), we
    act as your processor: we process it only on your documented instructions and
    as needed to provide the service, apply appropriate safeguards, and use
    sub-processors as described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. You
    are responsible for the lawfulness of the data you instruct us to process.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Suspension and termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may cancel at any time as described in the
    <a href="/refunds/">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>. We may suspend or
    terminate your access if you breach these Terms, fail to pay, or use the
    service unlawfully or in a way that risks harm to others or to the service.
    On termination, your right to use the service ends and we will handle your
    data as described in the Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL.jurisdiction}, without regard
    to conflict-of-law rules. The courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} will have
    jurisdiction over disputes, except where mandatory consumer-protection law
    gives you the right to bring a claim where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes take effect on
    the updated effective date above, and your continued use of the service means
    you accept them. If you do not agree, stop using the service and cancel.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. These
    Terms are entered into with {op}, {LEGAL.operatorDescriptor}.
  </p>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Not legal advice.</strong> This document is a starting point and
      not a substitute for review by a qualified attorney. Given that DummyLead
      records calls across borders, have counsel confirm your recording-consent
      and consumer-protection obligations before relying on these Terms.
    </p>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
